# Delegation: Student has-a BasePerson

`+BasePerson` is an owned component. Construction nests it. Student is not a
BasePerson for slot typing — add a sum if you want a shared type.

Target talks to Student as if it had BasePerson's fields and methods:

- `s.name` and `s.age` are promoted fields
- `s.greet()` is the promoted BasePerson method
- `s.rename` must be written on Student because BasePerson::rename returns a BasePerson

## Schema

```
Student = String/id +BasePerson
BasePerson = String/name Int/age

```

## Construction

```
[:Student "s17" [:BasePerson "Ada" 36]]
```

## Methods

```
BasePerson::greet = { "Hello {name}".tpl({String:String "name":name })}

BasePerson::rename = { String/n | [:BasePerson n age] }

Student::rename = { String/n | [:Student | name = n] }
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var s = StudentAssemblage.factory();
    trace(s.name);
    trace(s.greet());
    var next = s.rename("Grace");
    trace(next.name);
    trace(next.id);
}
```
